1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,610
The shop is down.

2
00:00:01,610 --> 00:00:03,437
Customers see an empty page.

3
00:00:03,437 --> 00:00:06,896
Your manager asks one question: which part is broken,

4
00:00:06,896 --> 00:00:08,201
and how do you know?

5
00:00:08,751 --> 00:00:13,073
This is the mastery lesson for application architecture and A P Is.

6
00:00:13,073 --> 00:00:15,007
You have learned eight skills.

7
00:00:15,007 --> 00:00:16,878
Now you prove them on a real,

8
00:00:16,878 --> 00:00:17,652
broken shop,

9
00:00:17,652 --> 00:00:18,361
with a lab,

10
00:00:18,361 --> 00:00:19,006
a checker,

11
00:00:19,006 --> 00:00:19,845
and a report.

12
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:23,360
I will fix the first fault live. You fix the other three.

13
00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:26,392
Meet Cloud Cart,

14
00:00:26,392 --> 00:00:27,988
released with four faults.

15
00:00:27,988 --> 00:00:29,523
Here is the map you drew,

16
00:00:29,523 --> 00:00:31,426
with a red pin on each problem.

17
00:00:31,976 --> 00:00:36,861
Pin one, on the API: it listens on the wrong port. That is configuration.

18
00:00:37,411 --> 00:00:41,891
Pin two, on the database: the file is missing, so the shop is not ready.

19
00:00:42,441 --> 00:00:47,284
Pin three, on the secrets file: it is readable by everyone. That is security.

20
00:00:47,834 --> 00:00:48,387
Pin four,

21
00:00:48,387 --> 00:00:53,359
on the request path: nobody can show one request travelling through both diaries.

22
00:00:53,909 --> 00:00:57,749
The checker prints pass or fail for four checks, and all four fail.

23
00:00:58,299 --> 00:01:01,649
Your mission: four pass lines, with proof for every fix.

24
00:01:03,699 --> 00:01:07,902
Before we start, here is where everything lives. It is also in the description.

25
00:01:08,452 --> 00:01:14,126
The repository is git hub dot com, slash it dash waves, slash dev ops dash A I.

26
00:01:14,676 --> 00:01:17,894
The lab is one file: lab seventy-five dot S H,

27
00:01:17,894 --> 00:01:20,132
in the academy slash lab folder.

28
00:01:20,132 --> 00:01:25,727
Your report template and install notes are in academy slash lesson seventy-five.

29
00:01:26,277 --> 00:01:28,158
Install it in three steps.

30
00:01:28,158 --> 00:01:29,677
Clone the repository.

31
00:01:29,677 --> 00:01:31,196
Go to the lab folder.

32
00:01:31,196 --> 00:01:35,536
Install the script into slash U S R slash local slash S bin.

33
00:01:36,086 --> 00:01:38,107
Three commands run everything.

34
00:01:38,107 --> 00:01:39,926
Lab up builds the problems.

35
00:01:39,926 --> 00:01:42,554
Lab check prints pass or fail for each.

36
00:01:42,554 --> 00:01:44,171
Lab down removes it all.

37
00:01:44,721 --> 00:01:46,114
Lab is a short name.

38
00:01:46,114 --> 00:01:47,925
Source the shortcuts file,

39
00:01:47,925 --> 00:01:49,249
and it runs sue do,

40
00:01:49,249 --> 00:01:50,990
lab seventy-five dot S H,

41
00:01:50,990 --> 00:01:51,548
for you.

42
00:01:52,098 --> 00:01:54,931
You need an Ubuntu virtual machine with root,

43
00:01:54,931 --> 00:01:56,317
python three and curl.

44
00:01:56,317 --> 00:01:59,213
It uses ports five thousand and eighty eighty.

45
00:01:59,213 --> 00:02:01,228
Run it only in your own machine.

46
00:02:03,578 --> 00:02:04,510
Now for real.

47
00:02:04,510 --> 00:02:06,589
I have cloned the repository,

48
00:02:06,589 --> 00:02:09,814
and the lab files are in a folder called lab.

49
00:02:09,814 --> 00:02:10,459
Type: CD,

50
00:02:10,459 --> 00:02:10,746
lab.

51
00:02:11,296 --> 00:02:13,451
List what is here. Type: L S.

52
00:02:14,001 --> 00:02:17,068
The lab script and the shortcuts file.

53
00:02:17,068 --> 00:02:18,602
Install the script.

54
00:02:18,602 --> 00:02:19,651
Type: sue do,

55
00:02:19,651 --> 00:02:20,297
install,

56
00:02:20,297 --> 00:02:20,862
dash m,

57
00:02:20,862 --> 00:02:22,154
seven five five,

58
00:02:22,154 --> 00:02:24,172
lab seventy-five dot S H,

59
00:02:24,172 --> 00:02:27,078
slash U S R slash local slash S bin.

60
00:02:27,628 --> 00:02:32,492
Load the short names. Type: source, shortcuts seventy-five dot S H.

61
00:02:33,042 --> 00:02:35,069
Build the lab. Type: lab up.

62
00:02:37,619 --> 00:02:40,200
Now ask the checker. Type: lab check.

63
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:45,910
Four FAIL lines. That is your starting point. Copy them into your report.

64
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,709
Keep four notes for every fault.

65
00:02:50,259 --> 00:02:55,059
One: the symptom, in the exact words of the output, or the exact wrong answer.

66
00:02:55,609 --> 00:02:58,041
Two: the cause, and the command that proved it.

67
00:02:58,591 --> 00:03:00,874
Three: the fix. One change only.

68
00:03:01,424 --> 00:03:03,856
Four: the proof, the output after the fix.

69
00:03:04,406 --> 00:03:06,561
Notes turn a lucky fix into evidence.

70
00:03:08,611 --> 00:03:09,345
Fault one,

71
00:03:09,345 --> 00:03:09,713
live.

72
00:03:09,713 --> 00:03:12,724
The checker says the API does not answer.

73
00:03:12,724 --> 00:03:13,825
Go to the shop.

74
00:03:13,825 --> 00:03:14,486
Type: CD,

75
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:15,221
slash opt,

76
00:03:15,221 --> 00:03:16,910
slash lab seventy-five.

77
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:21,961
Method first: ask each layer. Type: dot slash layers dot S H.

78
00:03:22,511 --> 00:03:23,161
Note one,

79
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:24,028
the symptom.

80
00:03:24,028 --> 00:03:25,545
The web page answers.

81
00:03:25,545 --> 00:03:30,746
The API gives zero zero zero: nobody is listening on port five thousand.

82
00:03:31,296 --> 00:03:34,858
Who is listening, then? Type: S S, dash L T N.

83
00:03:35,408 --> 00:03:37,918
Port eighty eighty is the web service.

84
00:03:37,918 --> 00:03:40,361
And something listens on fifty fifty,

85
00:03:40,361 --> 00:03:41,549
not five thousand.

86
00:03:41,549 --> 00:03:42,144
Note two,

87
00:03:42,144 --> 00:03:45,115
the cause: the API started on the wrong port.

88
00:03:45,665 --> 00:03:49,526
Where does the port come from? Type: grep, port, app dot conf.

89
00:03:50,076 --> 00:03:55,388
There it is: port equals fifty fifty. The configuration is wrong. The code is fine.

90
00:03:55,938 --> 00:03:56,769
Note three,

91
00:03:56,769 --> 00:03:57,374
the fix.

92
00:03:57,374 --> 00:03:58,583
One change only.

93
00:03:58,583 --> 00:03:59,338
Type: sed,

94
00:03:59,338 --> 00:03:59,867
dash I,

95
00:03:59,867 --> 00:04:03,796
then a substitution that sets port to five thousand,

96
00:04:03,796 --> 00:04:05,005
in app dot conf.

97
00:04:05,555 --> 00:04:08,926
A running program does not re-read its settings.

98
00:04:08,926 --> 00:04:09,699
Restart it.

99
00:04:09,699 --> 00:04:11,806
Type: dot slash start dot S H.

100
00:04:13,856 --> 00:04:19,168
Note four, the proof. Ask each layer again. Type: dot slash layers dot S H.

101
00:04:19,718 --> 00:04:20,992
The API now answers,

102
00:04:20,992 --> 00:04:22,457
but with five oh three,

103
00:04:22,457 --> 00:04:23,095
not ready.

104
00:04:23,095 --> 00:04:24,369
The symptom changed,

105
00:04:24,369 --> 00:04:27,236
and that is progress: this is the next fault,

106
00:04:27,236 --> 00:04:28,447
and the next layer,

107
00:04:28,447 --> 00:04:29,275
the database.

108
00:04:29,825 --> 00:04:32,406
Now ask the checker. Type: lab check.

109
00:04:32,956 --> 00:04:33,542
One PASS,

110
00:04:33,542 --> 00:04:34,258
three FAIL.

111
00:04:34,258 --> 00:04:35,235
One fault down,

112
00:04:35,235 --> 00:04:35,951
one change,

113
00:04:35,951 --> 00:04:36,667
with proof.

114
00:04:36,667 --> 00:04:39,271
Now it is your turn for the other three.

115
00:04:41,321 --> 00:04:45,097
Your report has five parts. The template is in the lesson folder.

116
00:04:45,647 --> 00:04:47,780
Setup: the checker output at the start.

117
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:49,952
Each fault, with its four notes.

118
00:04:50,502 --> 00:04:53,659
The final checker output, all four lines saying pass.

119
00:04:54,209 --> 00:04:55,337
Where you got stuck,

120
00:04:55,337 --> 00:04:56,522
and what unstuck you.

121
00:04:56,522 --> 00:04:59,286
Honest notes are worth more than a perfect story.

122
00:04:59,836 --> 00:05:01,906
And the cleanup proof, which we do next.

123
00:05:03,856 --> 00:05:05,044
Your three faults.

124
00:05:05,044 --> 00:05:05,836
No spoilers,

125
00:05:05,836 --> 00:05:06,892
only directions.

126
00:05:06,892 --> 00:05:08,872
And remember: after every fix,

127
00:05:08,872 --> 00:05:10,258
ask the layers again,

128
00:05:10,258 --> 00:05:13,029
because the next symptom is the next clue.

129
00:05:13,579 --> 00:05:16,299
Check two: the API answers but is not ready.

130
00:05:16,299 --> 00:05:18,091
Which endpoint tells you why?

131
00:05:18,091 --> 00:05:21,737
Look in the lab folder for the file the database should be,

132
00:05:21,737 --> 00:05:24,085
and think about what changed its name.

133
00:05:24,085 --> 00:05:25,569
Fix it with one command.

134
00:05:26,119 --> 00:05:28,879
Check three: a secrets file must be private.

135
00:05:28,879 --> 00:05:30,385
Read its mode with stat,

136
00:05:30,385 --> 00:05:34,401
and compare it with what the rubric of the security lesson said.

137
00:05:34,401 --> 00:05:35,719
One command fixes it.

138
00:05:36,269 --> 00:05:38,100
Check four: log in as alice,

139
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:40,716
with the password from the secrets file,

140
00:05:40,716 --> 00:05:41,959
and keep the token.

141
00:05:41,959 --> 00:05:46,537
Call the orders endpoint with that token and the label M C zero eight.

142
00:05:46,537 --> 00:05:48,957
Request the page with the same label.

143
00:05:48,957 --> 00:05:51,507
Then search both diaries for the label,

144
00:05:51,507 --> 00:05:54,189
and save what you find in trace dot text.

145
00:05:54,739 --> 00:05:58,984
Same method every time: symptom, layer, fix one thing, verify.

146
00:06:01,034 --> 00:06:04,426
When you finish, clean up, and prove it. Type: lab down.

147
00:06:05,976 --> 00:06:11,672
Proof one: is the lab folder gone? Type: L S, slash opt, slash lab seventy-five.

148
00:06:12,222 --> 00:06:14,270
No such file or directory.

149
00:06:14,270 --> 00:06:16,396
Proof two: count it in opt.

150
00:06:16,396 --> 00:06:17,183
Type: L S,

151
00:06:17,183 --> 00:06:17,971
slash opt,

152
00:06:17,971 --> 00:06:18,365
pipe,

153
00:06:18,365 --> 00:06:19,310
grep dash c,

154
00:06:19,310 --> 00:06:20,649
lab seventy-five.

155
00:06:21,199 --> 00:06:23,737
Zero. Now remove the lab script itself.

156
00:06:24,287 --> 00:06:31,477
Type: sue do, R M, slash U S R slash local slash S bin slash lab seventy-five dot S H.

157
00:06:32,027 --> 00:06:35,223
Proof three: is anything left in S bin?

158
00:06:35,223 --> 00:06:36,042
Type: L S,

159
00:06:36,042 --> 00:06:38,993
slash U S R slash local slash S bin,

160
00:06:38,993 --> 00:06:39,403
pipe,

161
00:06:39,403 --> 00:06:39,730
W C,

162
00:06:39,730 --> 00:06:40,304
dash l.

163
00:06:40,854 --> 00:06:41,622
Zero.

164
00:06:42,172 --> 00:06:46,581
Proof four: is anything still listening on port eighty eighty?

165
00:06:46,581 --> 00:06:47,292
Type: S S,

166
00:06:47,292 --> 00:06:48,074
dash L T N,

167
00:06:48,074 --> 00:06:48,430
pipe,

168
00:06:48,430 --> 00:06:49,283
grep dash c,

169
00:06:49,283 --> 00:06:50,279
eighty eighty.

170
00:06:50,829 --> 00:06:51,510
Zero again.

171
00:06:51,510 --> 00:06:52,749
The shop is stopped,

172
00:06:52,749 --> 00:06:54,359
and everything is removed.

173
00:06:54,359 --> 00:06:56,589
Paste these proofs into your report.

174
00:06:58,639 --> 00:07:02,564
Here is how your work is judged. Six points, and you need all six.

175
00:07:03,114 --> 00:07:04,949
The checker shows four pass lines.

176
00:07:05,499 --> 00:07:08,699
Every fault has a symptom, a cause, a fix, and a proof.

177
00:07:09,249 --> 00:07:10,998
You changed one thing at a time.

178
00:07:11,548 --> 00:07:14,364
The report is complete, including where you got stuck.

179
00:07:14,914 --> 00:07:18,733
The cleanup proof shows nothing left behind, and nothing still listening.

180
00:07:19,283 --> 00:07:21,672
You ran it only in your own virtual machine.

181
00:07:22,222 --> 00:07:23,844
To pass, you need all six.

182
00:07:25,894 --> 00:07:31,761
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine. Take your time. Mastery is slow and exact.

183
00:07:32,311 --> 00:07:35,084
One: clone the repository and install the lab.

184
00:07:35,634 --> 00:07:38,450
Two: run lab up, and save the checker output.

185
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:42,221
Three: fix the three remaining faults, with four notes each.

186
00:07:42,771 --> 00:07:44,883
Four: write the report from the template.

187
00:07:45,433 --> 00:07:48,612
Five: run the checker. All four lines must say pass.

188
00:07:49,162 --> 00:07:51,125
Six: clean up, and paste the proof.

189
00:07:51,675 --> 00:07:53,509
Pause the video, and begin now.

190
00:08:09,059 --> 00:08:09,934
Quick check.

191
00:08:10,484 --> 00:08:14,260
Which layer do you suspect when the page loads but no products appear?

192
00:08:14,810 --> 00:08:18,372
Why does a fix sometimes change the symptom instead of ending it?

193
00:08:18,922 --> 00:08:21,013
What does one request label let you do?

194
00:08:21,563 --> 00:08:23,120
What proves your cleanup worked?

195
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:26,520
Mastery evidence covered: M C zero eight,

196
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:29,021
building on objectives one to eight,

197
00:08:29,021 --> 00:08:32,844
in the application architecture and A P Is masterclass.

198
00:08:33,394 --> 00:08:35,463
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

199
00:08:46,013 --> 00:08:47,741
Next: the next masterclass.

